{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_53_75729873#11_135839513","relevance":3,"reason":"This textbook/PDF passage is dedicated to African cooperation and resistance in the Atlantic slave trade and directly states that many African rulers and merchants willingly participated, helped capture Africans, delivered them to Europeans, and received gold, guns, and goods; some rulers opposed it.","learned":"A textbook source frames African rulers' contribution as cooperation with merchants: helping capture enslaved Africans, facilitating coastal delivery to Europeans, and trading captives for goods, while some rulers resisted."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3414","reason":"This query is still producing highly direct evidence about African rulers' role; continue until the result quality drops or duplicates dominate."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3414"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_13195298#7_19215443","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3414","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_13195298#7_19215443\" , \"end_char\": 4371.000000 , \"headings\": \" \" , \"segment\": \"How did some African rulers participate in the <cover>slave trade? African rulers </cover>had a major role in the slave trade. They benefited from the slave trade by capturing control of the slave trade. They Bring people inland and transport them to the coast to sell to European traders. What was the triangular trade? The triangular trade, was a trade system between Europe, Africa, and the Americas. Europeans brought manufactured goods to Africa in return for slaves. From the Atlantic Ocean to the Americas, Africans were sold. Traders then returned to Europe with sugar, coffee, and tobacco. How did Africans change the Americas?\" , \"start_char\": 3749.000000 , \"title\": \"\" , \"url\": \"https://quizlet.com/64036061/biggsa_fgch20-flash-cards/\" }"}}
