{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"african kings\" \"transatlantic slave trade\" captured sold)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_1188371771#6_2248441439","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3417","rank":1,"snippet":"\"headings\": \"Effects of the Transatlantic Slave Trade (a Different View) Effects of the Transatlantic Slave Trade (a Different View) How the <cover>Transatlantic Slave Trade Began Who Shall We Blame for the Slave Trade? Could Things Have Turned Out Differently? What Were the Short-Term Effects of the Slave Trade? What Are the Long-Term Effects of the Transatlantic Trade? Are Apologies in Order? What Lesson Have We Learned? © 2018 artsofthetimes Comments \" , \"segment\": \"Looking at it from a different perspective, it is a good thing to know that Africans, many times, aided the trade too. As they captured and sold off natives who were mainly spoils of war, trading in slaves flourished and the more they intensified their efforts in supplying captured and banished natives to the willing buyers, all was good. It was simply a case of demand and supply. To address the issue of blame, the white slave traders many times got their supplies with ease and without hindrance from some African kings </cover>who supplied the slave traders with their native subjects to carry out raiding and capturing expeditions. Did the African kings even care that before being "}}
