{"latest_judgment":{"docno":null,"relevance":0,"reason":"The latest query returned no results, so there is no new document to judge.","learned":"The exact phrase 'role of African rulers' did not match available passages."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"triangular trade\" \"african rulers\" slaves europeans)","reason":"Search explicitly for triangular trade together with African rulers, slaves, and Europeans to find documents that tie rulers' contribution directly to the triangle trade framework."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"triangular trade\" \"african rulers\" slaves europeans)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_102743421#0_243647745","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3422","rank":3,"snippet":"slave trade Atlantic slave trade Introduction Origins The <cover>Triangular Trade Opposition to and End of the Slave Trade \" , \"segment\": \"Atlantic slave trade  - Students | Britannica Kids | Homework Help Atlantic slave trade Introduction Photos.com/Getty Images Beginning about 1500, millions of Black Africans were taken from their homes and sold into slavery in the New World. European colonial powers, working with African rulers, shipped their human cargo across the Atlantic Ocean to work on plantations in their American colonies. As many as 10 million people endured the forced journey, and many more died in transport. After nearly four centuries, humanitarian efforts finally brought an end to the Atlantic slave trade in the second half of the 1800s. Origins Slavery was practiced in Africa long before the arrival of Europeans on the continent. The practice was widespread both in the Islamic societies of North Africa and in the Black African states south of the Sahara. Black Africans were traded across the Sahara, across the Red Sea (from Ethiopia and Somalia), and out of East Africa to supply the Islamic world and the Indian Ocean region with slaves. </cover>In Europe, slavery had nearly died out in the ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_102743421#5_243655534","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_13195298#7_19215443","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"13/50"}}
